> - Hardware + software integrated solution with three deployment models
> - AI Butler system for autonomous server operations
> - SME product line for small and medium enterprises
> - Reference deployment verified on dedicated production infrastructure

---

## Executive Summary

Canada.ca operates on Adobe AEM, a platform selected over a decade ago for a world without modern search, AI. Today, that architecture presents well-known challenges: **$Millions in annual total costs**, **a delayed publish pipeline**, **difficult to migrate new department content**, and **no native database, search, or AI capabilities** — all of which must be outsourced to separate vendors.

We offer a fundamentally different approach — not a proposal for a future system, but a **working, verifiable platform** built today:

> **Designed by 20 years of Canada.ca experience. Developed by an AI-empowered team. Verifiable on demand. Operationally proven.**

**What's new: Our platform is now available as a complete hardware + software appliance**, pre-configured and ready to deploy. Three delivery models:

| Model | Description | Best For |
|---|---|---|
| **On-Premise Appliance** | Pre-configured server with WebBot + FileBot + AI Butler, shipped to client site | Security-first government departments, air-gapped environments |
| **Managed Service** | We host, maintain, and operate the platform; client accesses via secure portal | Organizations without dedicated IT operations |
| **Hybrid Cloud** | Admin/cms runs on local appliance; public site served through cloud CDN | Maximum performance + security balance |

