## 5. Three Deployment Models (NEW)

### 5.1 On-Premise Appliance

A pre-configured server shipped directly to the client. Plug in, power on, and the system is ready — no setup, no configuration.

**Specification:**
- Ubuntu 24.04 LTS pre-installed
- Docker containers for all services (WebBot, FileBot, nginx, PostgreSQL)
- AI Butler pre-configured with client's contact methods
- SSL certificates pre-generated (or client CA)
- Admin interface accessible via local network only
- Optional: static HTML publish to cloud CDN for public access

**Ideal for:**
- Government departments requiring strict data sovereignty
- Air-gapped / classified environments
- Organizations without dedicated IT infrastructure

**Delivery:**
- Physical server shipped with installation guide (one page)
- Remote handover session with AI Butler introduction (1 hour)
- Ongoing: AI Butler handles maintenance; human reviews changes

### 5.2 Managed Service

We host and operate the platform on dedicated infrastructure. Client accesses WebBot CMS via secure HTTPS portal.

**Specification:**
- Dedicated server per client (not shared tenant)
- Managed via AI Butler (our ops team reviews critical changes)
- Regular backups with verification (AI Butler automated)
- 99.9% uptime SLA
- Security patches applied within 48h of release
- Monthly operations review report (AI Butler generated)

**Ideal for:**
- Organizations without dedicated IT staff
- SMEs wanting enterprise CMS without enterprise overhead
- Rapid deployment (no hardware procurement delay)

**Pricing model:**
- Monthly subscription (hardware + software + ops included)
- No upfront hardware cost
- Scalable: upgrade server specs as content grows

### 5.3 Hybrid (Cloud + Local)

The recommended model for Canada.ca — local CMS admin for security, cloud CDN for public performance.

**Architecture:**
```
┌─────────────────────┐        ┌─────────────────────────┐
│ Client Site         │        │ Cloud                   │
│                     │        │                         │
│ WebBot CMS (Admin)  │───────►│ Publish Server (static) │
│ FileBot Assets      │  sync  │ CDN (Cloudflare, etc.)  │
│ AI Butler (ops)     │        │                         │
│ PostgreSQL (data)   │        │ No API exposure         │
│                     │        │ Cache-only delivery     │
│Internal network only│        │ Global acceleration     │
└─────────────────────┘        └─────────────────────────┘
```

**Benefits:**
- **Security**: Admin interface never exposed to internet
- **Performance**: Public site accelerated via CDN, global
- **Cost**: Cloud only for bandwidth+storage (not compute)
- **Control**: Full data ownership on local appliance
- **Scaling**: CDN handles traffic spikes automatically

### 5.4 Decision Matrix

| Requirement | On-Premise | Managed | Hybrid |
|---|---|---|---|
| Data never leaves client site | ✅ Fully | ❌ Hosted by us | ✅ Admin data local |
| No upfront hardware cost | ❌ Must buy server | ✅ Subscription | ✅ Server + cloud |
| Global public access | ❌ Local bandwidth only | ✅ Cloud CDN | ✅ Cloud CDN |
| Air-gap / classified | ✅ Fully isolated | ❌ Internet required | ❌ Needs cloud sync |
| No IT staff needed | ❌ Some local IT needed | ✅ Full managed | ⚠️ Hybrid admin |
| Fastest deployment | ⚠️ Hardware shipping | ✅ Immediate | ⚠️ Hardware + config |
| Lowest total cost | ✅ One-time + minimal ops | ✅ Predictable monthly | ⚠️ Hardware + cloud |

