## 6. AI Butler — Detailed Design (NEW)

### 6.1 Architecture

The AI Butler (OpenClaw Gateway) runs as a service on the server, with:

```
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                   AI BUTLER                           │
│                                                       │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐      │
│  │ Gateway Agent (OpenClaw Gateway)            │      │
│  │  • Receives natural language commands       │      │
│  │  • Plans & executes operations              │      │
│  │  • Requests human approval for critical ops │      │
│  │  • Logs every action to audit trail         │      │
│  └──────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘      │
│             │                                         │
│    ┌────────┼────────┬────────┬────────┐              │
│    ▼        ▼        ▼        ▼        ▼              │
│ ┌──────┐ ┌──────┐ ┌──────┐ ┌──────┐ ┌──────┐          │
│ │System│ │Docker│ │Post- │ │Backup│ │Log   │          │
│ │  OS  │ │      │ │greSQL│ │      │ │Watch │          │
│ └──────┘ └──────┘ └──────┘ └──────┘ └──────┘          │
│                                                       │
│ Communication:                                        │
│ • Telegram/Signal/Email — send alerts &               │
│   request approvals                                   │
│ • SSH — execute server commands                       │
│ • Docker API — manage containers                      │
│ • PostgreSQL — query database health                  │
│ • HTTP — check service health endpoints               │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 6.2 Capabilities

| Category | Tasks | Frequency | Human Approval? |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Monitoring** | Process health, port status, disk usage, memory | Every 30 min | No (alert only) |
| **Security** | CVE scan, SSL expiry check, login attempt audit | Daily | No (alert only) |
| **Backups** | Full DB dump, config backup, integrity verify | Daily | No (report only) |
| **Patching** | OS updates, Docker image updates, Python deps | Weekly | Yes |
| **Configuration** | nginx config changes, env var updates | On demand | Yes |
| **Incident Response** | Service restart, disk cleanup, failover | On demand | Yes (critical) |

### 6.3 Human-in-the-Loop Workflow

```
1. AI Butler detects or receives a task
2. AI Butler: Analyzes impact, plans steps, estimates risk
3. AI Butler: Presents plan to human (via Telegram/Signal)
4. Human: Reviews and approves, modifies, or rejects
5. AI Butler: Executes with full logging
6. AI Butler: Verifies success, reports outcome
7. AI Butler: Generates audit entry

Exception: Emergency auto-remediation for non-critical issues:
  - Restart a crashed non-critical service → auto, notify
  - Clear a full temp directory → auto, notify
  - Critical service crash → alert human, wait for instruction
```

### 6.4 Cost Impact

| Before AI Butler | After AI Butler |
|---|---|
| Dedicated sysadmin: $80-120k/yr | AI Butler: $0 (open-source) |
| Human error rate: ~5-10% of ops | Human error: near zero (AI executes) |
| Incident response: 30-60 min avg | Incident triage: <1 min (AI detects) |
| Audit compliance: manual log collection | Audit: auto-generated, complete |

### 6.5 Technical Implementation

- **Platform**: OpenClaw Gateway (open-source, Node.js)
- **Model**: DeepSeek Reasoner (cost-effective, high reasoning)
- **Channel**: Telegram (alerts, approval requests, reports)
- **Tools**: SSH, Docker API, HTTP health checks, PostgreSQL client
- **Security**: All commands logged; destructive ops require explicit human approval
- **Backup**: Configuration managed as code (git-tracked)

